    <description>             A low-pressure recirculating wind tunnel. The wind tunnels are used for the multi-disciplinary scientific              study of aerosol formation and transport (on Mars and Earth), granular electrification, magnetic properties,             erosion, cohesion/adhesion, water transport, UV induced mineralogy, bacterial survival and much more. The              wind tunnels are accessible to national and international collaborators and space agencies for scientific              experiments, instrument testing, calibration and qualification. The wind tunnels have been financed by              Aarhus University, the European Space Agency (ESA) and the Villum Kann Rasmussen Foundation.          </description>
